{# An American-style "work in progress" barricade planted on a zone under works
   (§ délais): a low, wide board with diagonal black/amber hazard stripes on two
   splayed A-frame legs, captioned with the phase. `phase` picks the local
   variant class (CVA-manuel, cf. CLAUDE.md §7) AND the caption: both phases are
   fully opaque — planned ("Travaux à venir", during the lead: a chantier is
   reserved here, also why some tree choices are blocked) is static; active
   ("Travaux en cours", the pose: the artisan is on site) gets a flashing amber
   beacon and a slight bob. Origin = ground midpoint between the two feet; the
   board stands above it, the caption sits below. Colours/motion live in
   scene.css. Non-clickable (pointer-events none) so the zone stays selectable. #}
{% props phase = 'planned' %}
{% set label = phase == 'active' ? 'Travaux en cours' : 'Travaux à venir' %}
<g class="chantier-marker chantier-marker--{{ phase }}"{{ attributes }}>
    <path class="cm-legs" d="M-15 -19 L-27 -1 M15 -19 L27 -1"/>
    <rect class="cm-board" x="-32" y="-33" width="64" height="13" rx="2"/>
    <circle class="cm-beacon" cx="0" cy="-37" r="3.2"/>
    <text class="cm-label" x="0" y="15" text-anchor="middle">{{ label }}</text>
</g>
